      "proof_summary": "Preserve arbitrary fields F,K with their algebra structure, algebraic closedness of K, DecidableEq K, an elliptic Weierstrass curve W over F, and natural n with its cast in K nonzero. Retain existence of the K-unit-valued pairing on the full n-torsion submodule of the K-base-changed curve, with all five original conjuncts: exact first- and second-variable multiplicative bilinearity, self-pairing equal to one, covariance under every F-algebra automorphism of K, and full first-variable nondegeneracy quantified over every torsion point. Preserve the complete 88-line supplier source, including the helper transferring the raw pairing laws to the torsion submodule and deriving skew symmetry to transfer right nondegeneracy to the stated first-variable conclusion. The main proof internally establishes ellipticity of the base change and the Dedekind-domain coordinate ring, uses all four verified Weil-pairing laws, and proves right nondegeneracy from translation invariance, the full Weil-function valuation formula, and the valuation bound for multiplication pullback. No prime-n, characteristic-zero, finite-extension, exact-order, nonzero-point or extra Dedekind-domain hypothesis is added, and no conclusion is weakened.",
